yes(342,'B','The carbonate amount is 0.1×(10/1000) = 0.001 mol. Acid converts each CO₃²⁻ into one CO₂ molecule, so the CO₂ amount is also 0.001 mol. Its STP volume is 0.001×22.4 = 0.0224 dm³, or 22.4 cm³.',[RX],question='What volume of CO₂ at STP results when 10 cm³ of 0.1 mol dm⁻³ Na₂CO₃ solution reacts with excess acid? [Molar gas volume at STP = 22.4 dm³ mol⁻¹]',options=['2.240 cm³','22.40 cm³','224.0 cm³','2240 cm³'],audit='Corrected oldA toB and removed contradictory final arithmetic; completed supplied molar-volume unit.',check='carbonate-volume')
